Test 1 
Root cause:   The test was using an incorrect placeholder locator. 
It searched for "User Name", but the login input on the page has the placeholder "Username". 
As a result, Playwright could not find the element and timed out while waiting for it.

Fix:          Changed the locator from:
              page.getByPlaceholder("User Name")
              to:
              page.getByPlaceholder("Username")

How I verified: Ran `npx playwright test --headed` and confirmed the test passes.

Test 2 
Root cause:   The test used an incorrect assertion locator and expected text. 
It searched for an element via getByTestId("error"), but the page does not expose the error message through a matching 
test id. The actual error message displayed after a failed login is
 "Epic sadface: Username and password do not match any user in this service".

Fix:          Replaced the assertion with:
              await expect(
                page.getByText(
                  "Epic sadface: Username and password do not match any user in this service"
                )
              ).toBeVisible();

How I verified: Ran `npx playwright test --headed` and confirmed the test passes.

Test 3
Root cause:   The click action was not awaited. 
Although the test currently passes because the assertion retries until the cart badge updates, 
the test relies on asynchronous timing and may become flaky.

Fix:          Added the missing await before the click action:
              await page.locator('[data-test="add-to-cart-sauce-labs-backpack"]').click();

How I verified: Ran `npx playwright test --headed` and confirmed the test passes.